source: workspace/acyclic-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help.stdout
---
The acyclic tracker. Every command prints one JSON document when piped and text for people at a terminal (`-o` chooses), except `prime`, `completions`, `import --schema` and help and version text. A command line that doesn't parse prints its error as text on standard error, whatever `-o` says

Usage: acyclic [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Command Groups:
  item         Adds, edits, shows, lists, finishes, reopens, archives and deletes items
  thread       Adds, edits, shows and lists threads, and finds, claims and releases ready work
  repository   Adds, edits, shows and lists repository records

Other Commands:
  needs        Lists what needs the user
  init         Sets up a tracker clone as a new replica, creating the repository if there is none
  sync         Fetches every replica's state from `origin`, joins it into this one, and pushes this replica's refs
  prime        Prints conventions for agents, matched to this version, as text
  import       Imports a plan, adding and updating what it names and never deleting; `--schema` prints an example
  doctor       Lists entities that can't be read
  serve        Serves the JSON API and the app, refusing any request without the user's Tailscale identity
  up           Serves the JSON API and the app on this machine, to whoever holds its session
  completions  Prints a completion script for a shell, as text

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global options:
      --tracker <TRACKER>  The tracker clone; otherwise `ACYCLIC_TRACKER`, else the clone you are in, else, in a Git repository, the mapping in ~/.config/acyclic/trackers.toml, whose default applies when no prefix matches
      --actor <ACTOR>      Who acts, as `kind/id` such as `session/mac`; otherwise `ACYCLIC_ACTOR`, else the user, `actor/user`
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>    How to print: the JSON envelope, or tables and summaries for people, with errors as text on standard error; otherwise pretty on a terminal and json when piped [possible values: json, pretty]

Run 'acyclic help <command>' for more information on a command.
